course: dictionary
lesson: 11928
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Calving is one of them. On a farm, calving is the birth of a calf. In geography, calving is when a big piece of ice breaks off the edge of a glacier and falls into the sea, making icebergs.
explain: The sentence tells you which meaning to use. «The farmer was up all night during calving season» is about cows and calves, so it means birth. «Huge chunks of ice fell from the calving glacier» is about ice, so it means breaking off.
explain: Check your meaning with the swap test: put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Calving season is the busy time when many calves are born, and farmers help if there is trouble.
fact: Calving has two meanings: the birth of a calf, and the breaking off of ice from a glacier into the sea.
fact: The verb forms are calve, calves, calved and calving, as in «The cow calved in the night.»
fact: «Calving season» is the busy time on a farm when many calves are born.
fact: A «calving glacier» loses huge pieces of ice into the sea, and those pieces become icebergs.
fact: Scientists watch calving closely: when glaciers calve more often, it can show they are melting faster.
exercise: «The farmer was up all night during calving season.» What does calving mean here? | A tall wooden fence | *The birth of calves | A cold wind over the hills | The breaking off of ice into the sea
exercise: «Huge chunks of ice fell from the calving glacier into the sea.» What does calving mean here? | The birth of a calf on a farm | A sunny day at the beach | Melting snow running down a hill | *The breaking off of ice from a glacier into the sea
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a baby cow: «The farmer checked the calf in the barn.» | farmer | barn | checked | *calf
test: Which phrase is about ice breaking off a glacier? | calving season | *calving glacier | a sunny field | a bale of hay
test: Calving on a glacier makes what? | Dry deserts | Sand dunes | Rain clouds | *Icebergs
exam: Why might more calving on a glacier be a warning sign? | *It can show the glacier is melting faster | It means the sea is getting dry | It means the calves are growing big | It means the farmer is happy with the harvest
